[01:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'some tips, much appreciated. Quick reminder first because I use these words all the time and people mix them up. A clip is one generation or a run. One video file coming out of the sampler.'

[02:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A shot is a camera setup. And here\'s the part that\'s confusing. One clip can hold several shots because H3 will cut by itself if you write the markers. My chase scene is three angles and it\'s'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a single generation. The project menu is where you handle your clips and much more before you have to save your clip as its own file individually. For this example, it would be 10 clips and reload your references were gone.'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You would have to drag your reference back every time. So now, add clip and look, same reference sheets, same canvas, same length, same mode. Because it\'s a film, the next clip is almost always the same'

[02:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people in the same room. The prompt doesn\'t carry over except subject definitions because that part just describes the references that came with it and I\'d only retype it. You can reorder them, rename them. And'

[02:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can disable a clip, that\'s this one here. That\'s for when clip six is good and clip seven is not. You switch seven off, you render the project again and it skips it. It\'s still in the file, it\'s just not in'

[03:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the run. And the project lives in the workflow itself. You reload your browser, it\'s still there. Save, open your project in the project menu. Load and save on the node is for a'

[03:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'single clip. You can import those individual clips into a project. There is an import option for that as well. Okay, so continuity. The problem is simple. You generate clip one in a room. You generate clip two in the same room,'

[03:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'same prompt, same reference sheet, but the placement of various things are different. Pipes moved, characters are placed in a completely different way. The eye catches it immediately on the cut. So this is the carry look.'

[03:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You drop the previous clip in and you pick a the 22 frames. That window gets handed to the model as the starting point. So, clip two doesn\'t invent the room, it already has it.'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And this is the part I want you to actually look at because it matters more than anything else in this video. Where you put that window changes everything. If the window is a face in shadow or motion blur or the camera'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whipping past, the model gets nothing useful and clip two goes somewhere else. So, I scrub and I look for a moment where the scene reads clearly. Something still. Something lit. So, for example, here is a gen with a'

[04:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'previous video loaded with 22 frames. Or even five frames can be good, too. And a generation without where you get a totally different layout and lose continuity. Right. So, doing that by hand for 10 or'

[04:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more clips is a lot of clicking. Render all does the whole project with an automatic carry look option. Before talking about the render all option in the project menu, I want to show you a 34-second clip with no cut at'

[04:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all. It has been done with the continue from video slot that allows you to make an infinite length clip without any seams even while the camera and subject is in motion.'

[05:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; So, that was an example with the'

[05:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'continue from video slot for clip extension. The noticeable thing is the music between the three assembled clip is not exactly the same. But still, it kept the same style. You can prepare your clips like I did'

[05:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here and choose the option chained in one continuous take with or without carry look enabled. The checkbox next to it, if enabled, it would also put the last video back in a regular slot and analyze the shot to get'

[06:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a clear image. But in this case, since I wanted a continuous shot with not cut, it wasn\'t the best option. One important thing to get the best result and avoid the two frames misalignment is to output your video at'

[06:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a 4:4:4 or 4:2:2. It\'s the subsampling. So, a 4:2:0 subsampling format would create a two-frame offset at the joint of the extension, which will result in some'

[06:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'visible seams. Since I render pretty much all at 4:4:4, I don\'t run into this issue. You can see in the continue [music] from video slot which chroma you\'re at. Green for anything equal or above 4:2:2'

[06:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and red in 4:2:0. For the recitation short movie, I used render all clip by clip and checked the carry look box. So, after each generation while I was away, the node'

[06:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'would automatically load the last clip in a regular video slot, scan the video, and select a piece of it, usually 22F based on exposure and how steady it is, avoiding the black bits and the blown'

[07:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'out bits. Now, it is not guaranteed. It\'s a score. Most of the time it lands on something sensible, and sometimes it picks a window I wouldn\'t have. If nothing in the clip reads well, it'

[07:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'says so right there in orange, weak span. Sound stays off on a carry, by the way. Same room does not mean same soundtrack. And if you\'re not doing a whole project, say you just made one clip and you want'

[07:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the next one to match, there\'s a last render button right on the video slot. I also tried different things to speed up the render. I usually render the final output at 30 steps with Sage attention 2.2 only. The new kitchen attention seems great without the need'

[07:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to install all the dependencies, but since I use the easy comfy UI installer, it is all automatic. In the ref 2 video model, I think only H3 spectrum worth the trade in quality with around 40% increase in speed.'

[07:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
